{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/122112-freeholds-of-the-world","id":122112,"title":"Freeholds of the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-29T17:56:32-07:00","id":122112,"title":"Freeholds of the World","content":"I've made no secret of my love for the international domains presented in <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, and have high hopes for similar sections in the future Chronicle books. Regardless of whether or not Changeling eventually gets the GMC treatment, it remains very much a game not tied to the familiar Western world at all; the myths of every culture have space in Arcadia, and even simple urban legends and folk traditions can take on a life of their own beyond the Thorns. The Lost are not a strictly local phenomenon, and have every reason to have sizable presences across the globe. We've seen the Directional Courts of Asia and the Sun-Moon dichotomy of Slavic lands, and smaller, stranger paradigms must certainly exist as well.<br /> <br /> The question is simple; what cities would you like to see?<br /> <br /> First on my list is Hong Kong. It's a bustling city, one of the central hubs of international finance; it's essential to the world economy. From Chinese hands to the British and back again (and now in an odd state of partial independence), Hong Kong has a shifting, contrary identity. Its people are distinct from any nationality beyond their city, and most are bi- or tri-lingual. Chinese folklore and tradition coexist with Christianity and even Islam; neon floods the streets at night. There's crime here to rival the big business, and lots of hands moving behind the scenes. I see the Seasonal Courts (brought in by the British) in decline and forced to peacefully (or perhaps not-so-peacefully) coexist with the ascendant Directional Courts. The Lost of Hong Kong have a dizzying variety of forms - here are dragons of old walking alongside the city lights incarnate, a hopping corpse looking for a grave he doesn't have and a spirit of the old forests that still stand calling each other friends - all struggling to get by in one of the fastest-changing locales on the planet.<br /> <br /> Far away from there is Cairo, a city with history that stretches back longer than the oldest memory; images of Egypt under the pharaohs (and the strange animal-headed gods they deified) wrestle with the legends of Greek and Roman conquerors, a Biblical past, and the rise of Islam. At the same time, a new spirit has overtaken the city, a flashpoint in a modern revolution that held the interest of the whole world. Cairo is then a place of contradictions, full of heirs to many ancient worlds and instead choosing to make their own in the image of freedom. There's violence and uncertainty and struggle, certainly, but there is hope, too. That's something the Lost identify with keenly. They embody all manner of shapes and sorts; a stone-faced <i>ushabti</i> rebels from an eternity of servitude to a dead king, a brave leader takes on the horns of Alexander, a <i>jinn</i> peddles secrets and glows with smokeless fire, and all other sorts of strangeness. The Courts here could be interesting; the Sun and Moon Courts might draw on ancient solar traditions (Ra's daily struggle, or the heresy of Ahkenaten), or we could see something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T16:45:49-07:00","id":127076,"title":"","content":"While not half as developed as the previous two ideas, I wouldn't mind taking a swing at Kiev, just because you could draw from Slavic pagan folklore along with twisted Christianity and (I think??) Vikings paid the ancient Kiev some visits as well. Also a chance to use those lovely Sun/Moon Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:12:51-07:00","id":127517,"title":"","content":"I've always had a soft spot in my heart for Greco-Roman mythology, and I've always wanted to develop a Freehold where the courts are based around the worship of the Classical Pantheon of Gods. It would be easy to homebrew an adaptation to make the existing Seasonal Courts into Helenistic sub-cults (Summer to Ares/Mars, Spring to Aphrodite/Venus or Dionysus, etc.), but a real ground-up Freehold based on the Gods would be fantastic. I just don't have the time to do it myself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I ask for so little. Just fear me, <b>love me</b>, do as I say and I will be your slave.<br /> -Jareth, Goblin King","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2846-jhornb02","name":"jhornb02","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2846_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T16:19:51-07:00","id":130857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jhornb02</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/122112-freeholds-of-the-world?p=127517#post127517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always had a soft spot in my heart for Greco-Roman mythology, and I've always wanted to develop a Freehold where the courts are based around the worship of the Classical Pantheon of Gods. It would be easy to homebrew an adaptation to make the existing Seasonal Courts into Helenistic sub-cults (Summer to Ares/Mars, Spring to Aphrodite/Venus or Dionysus, etc.), but a real ground-up Freehold based on the Gods would be fantastic. I just don't have the time to do it myself...</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a few major cults ruling the freehold and then there's an angry minority of smaller, more niche cults? I could definitely dig it. You would also have some beautiful Changelings built from that mythology and could probably build some really rad Entitlements out of that. Would you go for Athens or another city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:29:10-07:00","id":138403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/122112-freeholds-of-the-world?p=127076#post127076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not half as developed as the previous two ideas, I wouldn't mind taking a swing at Kiev, just because you could draw from Slavic pagan folklore along with twisted Christianity and (I think??) Vikings paid the ancient Kiev some visits as well. Also a chance to use those lovely Sun/Moon Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vikings founded it, even, depending on who you believe. Early Russian history is fascinating and also impossible to have any idea of what's the more likely truth. <br /> <br /> My home town is... fairly uninteresting, except for one idea regarding it's parks and ravines. Toronto's a huge city, big metropolis, 4th biggest on the continent. But just as the Hedge has paths and trods running through it, Toronto has great ravines running through it that are safe passages of nature through the city. You can't build in them, because storms can flood them and erode away the land under the buildings; happened in the 50s once, an entire residential area was swept away. There's also the Islands, which are a third natural, a third residential, and a third airport. And High Park, a huge park that was given to the city on the grounds that it never be developed. Add that to it being one of the most multicultural cities in the world, up there in 2nd-language English speakers with London and New York, and there's lots of opportunity. We even have a fairy tale castle in Casa Lloma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T19:22:58-07:00","id":147449,"title":"","content":"Las Vegas seems like a city tailor-made for changelings. The neon lights, the extravagant casinos, the gamblers' emotions constantly running high, the sheer over-the-top-ness of everything... the city's (or, well, the Strip's) whole atmosphere is just made for them. The Courts of Spring and Winter would predominate; so many people go there hoping to win big, and so many are disappointed when they don't. (Incidentally, Vegas would be an interesting case of Winter doing well for itself in a hot landscape.)<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the local Courts deciding their leadership (and a million other things) through games of chance, which would be a major motif throughout the rest of the Freehold. The Goblin Market could be a special 'fairies only' casino; all those fantastic treasures you pay bizarre or unspeakable prices for in other freeholds, you can win for absolutely nothing. But if you lose, well, you'll lose far more than money, and the house always wins in the end.<br /> <br /> The True Fae could also fill a loan shark- or Faustian tempter-like role, in counterpoint to the hobgoblins as croupiers/casino owners. The Fae themselves don't gamble; leaving things to chance is for suckers. No, it's far more profitable to make deals with the desperate and the losers (mortal and changeling). Need those debts taken care of? Lost all memories of your loved one on that toss you were sure you'd win? Want to make sure that appalling thing you did really does stay in Vegas? They can take care of it. Just sign the dotted line, please...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}